      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T09:24:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that each of the sub-computation is similar to the corrsponding one in second pass.\nIs it possible that we refactor all of computations into a function by giving clear input and output?\n\nE.g.\nfor (i \u003c size) {\n  getValues(int i, Entry a)\n  Entry t \u003d generateFractionEntry(a, underlyingIfaceTotal, tunIfaceTotal);\n  totalList.add(t);\n}\n\nfor(t in totalList) {\n   for(iface in underlyingIface) {\n      tmpEntry \u003d generateFractionEntry(t, perInterfaceTotal[iface], underlyingIfaceTotal);\n      tmpEntry.iface \u003d iface;\n      ....\n   }\n}",
      "range": {
