      "writtenOn": "2019-03-25T21:28:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I strongly support Junyu\u0027s idea and predict the costs will be completely insignificant.\n\n- This is iterating on the interfaces, which are not numerous.\n- The cost of a static method call of this kind is in the single-digits nanoseconds.\n- ...and the JIT will inline any method that is called often enough to make any difference anyway.\n\nNote that Kotlin has inline functions, and makes it a warning to try and use it for expected performance gains (as opposed to the change of semantics this modifier supports, and not using them is how the compiler knows).\n\nHonestly considering the first point I don\u0027t even think creating an object would make any appreciable difference. But if you pass the recycled entry this is not even a consideration.",
      "parentUuid": "748eed41_b2a78ce3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1337,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1342,
        "endChar": 13
      },
